BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 244.00 Tm (Section 4: Firsthand Failure Modes, Traps & Economics Checks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 221.78 Tm (The most expensive failure is infrastructure collapse. The Smartlead 100,000-email operator warns that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.55 Tm (high-volume senders typically land in spam within two weeks, and has watched agencies lose every inbox) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 191.33 Tm (overnight by parking them all on one provider, which is why 200 inboxes get split 67 Google, 67 Outlook and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 176.10 Tm (the rest SMTP [C2lkX09G4h4 @ 00:08:16]. Matt Lucero adds that Google and Microsoft can suspend) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 160.88 Tm (accounts pushing around 10,000 a day, that SMTP through Mail Reef has no built-in cap but more variance,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 145.65 Tm (and that warm-up is not a cure-all because it cannot save you from spam reports [J8lvEnIHcLk @ 00:48:57].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 130.43 Tm (Sergio Perea of Boost Hero pins the root cause on per-inbox greed, the 50-to-150 creep that burns domains) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 115.20 Tm (with no warning light, and insists no sequencer fixes a bad list, weak offer or wrong ICP [lvp7ODzi7I8 @) Tj ET
